{"uid":"polarizability_v3.py","name":"polarizability_v3.py","qualname":"polarizability_v3.py","kind":"module","file":"polarizability_v3.py","line":1,"end_line":420,"language":"py","signature":"","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"polarizability_v3.py — Corrected with proper particle-conserving ansatz =======================================================================","description":"Root cause identified: The uccsd() function in molecular_sim.py implements\nsingles excitations incorrectly. For excitation (o→v), it does:\n    CNOT ladder → RY(v) → CNOT ladder inverse\nThis ADDS an electron at v without REMOVING from o, producing |1110⟩\ninstead of |0110⟩. The states reachable by uccsd never include |0110⟩\nor |1001⟩, which are exactly the states the dipole operator connects\nto |1100⟩ (HF). Hence <μ>=0 always, giving α=0.\n\nFix: Implement proper Givens-rotation-based singles that conserve\nparticle number. For adjacent qubits, Givens(o,v,θ) is:\n    CNOT(v,o) → RY(v, 2θ) → CNOT(v,o)\nThis rotates in the {|10⟩, |01⟩} subspace:\n    |1_o 0_v⟩ → cos(θ)|1_o 0_v⟩ + sin(θ)|0_o 1_v⟩\n\nFor non-adjacent qubits, we SWAP to make them adjacent, apply Givens,\nthen SWAP back. This preserves all quantum numbers.\n\nWe keep the doubles excitation from uccsd since it works correctly\n(verified: it produces |1100⟩↔|0011⟩ rotation properly).","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"","members":["polarizability_v3.py::VQEResult","polarizability_v3.py::givens_single_excitation","polarizability_v3.py::particle_conserving_ansatz","polarizability_v3.py::StarkEvaluator","polarizability_v3.py::DipoleOperatorBuilder","polarizability_v3.py::PolarizabilityCalculator"],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
